      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of other people's judgment feels unbearable, and the fear of that pitying gaze is a very real kind of pain. It makes sense that you'd want to avoid the humiliation of the descent. Instead of focusing on the inevitable crash, consider what small, immediate thing you could do to reclaim a sliver of control for yourself right now. Even a tiny act of self-care or setting a small boundary can be a way to assert your dignity against the chaos.",
      "source": "target",
